  "extraction_notes": [
    "The supplied datasheet is titled FDV303N Digital FET, N-Channel and identifies Fairchild Semiconductor on the document; the requested manufacturer field is preserved as onsemi.",
    "Transfer characteristics were digitized from the 25 \u00b0C curve in Fig. 5 at VDS = 5 V. The -55 \u00b0C and 125 \u00b0C curves were not included.",
    "Output/on-region curves were digitized from Fig. 1 for the published VGS values 1.5 V, 2.0 V, 2.5 V, 2.7 V, 3.0 V, 3.5 V, and 4.5 V. The figure is a typical electrical-characteristics plot and does not separately print a temperature condition; the datasheet electrical-characteristics heading specifies TA = 25 \u00b0C unless otherwise noted.",
    "Capacitance curves were digitized from Fig. 8 on logarithmic VDS and capacitance axes at VGS = 0 V and f = 1 MHz. The tabulated Ciss, Coss, and Crss values at VDS = 10 V are retained separately in specs.",
    "The RDS(ON) table publishes minimum and typical values for the 4.5 V and 2.7 V conditions, and minimum and typical values at 125 \u00b0C for the 4.5 V condition; no maximum RDS(ON) value is printed for these rows.",
    "The body-diode forward-voltage table publishes a minimum of 0.83 V and a maximum of 1.2 V at VGS = 0 V and IS = 0.5 A. The body_diode field uses the digitized 25 \u00b0C typical curve value; the tabulated bounds are recorded here because the schema has one body-diode value field.",
    "Only R\u03b8JA = 357 \u00b0C/W is published; R\u03b8JC is not published. No body-diode trr or Qrr is published. Gate-charge, thermal, safe-operating-area, and temperature-dependence plots are not represented because the schema has no dedicated fields for them."
  ],
